#!/usr/bin/env beg

Accept three CSV files, ORIGINAL, ALICE, and BOB, followed by a key column.
Match rows by unique key and columns by header name. The files must have the
same columns, in any order. Handle quoted commas and multiline fields.

Apply edits from either copy. Combine changes to different cells and accept
identical edits once. Include rows inserted on either side. Honor deletions
when the other side left the row unchanged or also deleted it.

If both sides assign different values to a cell, insert different rows under
the same key, or disagree between editing and deleting a row, report its key,
the affected column or row, and all three versions on stderr. Exit 1 and emit
no CSV. Report invalid inputs on stderr and exit 2.

On success, write merged CSV to stdout in the original column and row order.
Append new keys in ALICE's order, then any remaining new keys in BOB's order.
